ive to `jb.mergeParent` (the PR's own changes) instead of `BaseSHA`, so main's changes do not trip `diff_max_lines`. Refuse the round (needs-human, nothing pushed) if any `<<<<<<<`/`>>>>>>>` marker remains or `UnmergedPaths` is non-empty. Pass `MergeParent: jb.mergeParent` in the request. A non-done role file keeps ending needs-human through the existing path.\n6. `servecmd/merger.go`, `servecmd/reviewfix.go`, `servecmd/serve.go` (line ~486): build the reviewfix loop once and pass it as `Rounds` in `merger.Deps` (replace the \"deliberately unset\" comment). Keep the `reviewfix` loop registered as before. The issue also says \"starter config\": no conflict-round switch exists in config or in `initcmd` today (`Deps.Rounds` is the switch), and starter role files live under protected `.ard/` paths, so make no config or `initcmd` change unless the worker finds a real setting. If it does, note it on the PR.\n7. `docs/proposal.md` (lines ~160, ~332, ~378) and `docs/layout.md` if a file is listed there: replace the \"follow-up\" text with the conflict-round behaviour, add the worker conflict round and the merge-parent commit in the code lane. Update `committer` and `worker` `doc.go` comments if they describe the code lane or inputs.\n\n### Test plan\n\nTest command: `make test`, and `make lint`.\n\n- `gitx/merge_test.go` `TestMergeNoCommitConflict`: union conflict returns the path; `TestMergeNoCommitClean`: none; `TestUnmergedPathsAfterResolve`: empty; `TestMergeNoCommitOtherError`: bad ref errors.\n- `committer/code_test.go`: `TestCommitCodeMergeParent` (two parents, second is main tip, tree has resolved files and main's other files, lease push used); `TestCommitCodeMergeParentNotMainTip` (refused, nothing pushed); `TestCommitCodeMergeParentInvalid` (non-hex, with Create: `ErrInvalid`); `TestCommitCodeMergeLeftover` (unmerged path refused); `TestCommitCodeMergeForbiddenPath` (declared `.github/x` rejected by `CheckCodePath`); `TestCommitCodeMergeBranchMoved` (`ErrConflict`